  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to resilience, social cohesion and interfaith dialogue amongst conflict affected communities in Nigeria.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This 18-month exceptional assistance measure will aim at facilitating peace, reducing violence and enhancing resilience among conflict affected communities. In the Northwest, the action will build on the encouraging results of an EU pilot project in Katsina state, expanding to other states &#xbf; namely Sokoto and Zamfara - supporting community-based livelihoods, social cohesion and climate change adaptation projects. In the Middle Belt, support will focus on developing interfaith/intrafaith dialogue and mediation efforts as a means to swiftly de-conflict inter-community clashes that risk mounting in violence and intensity if left unattended. The action will strive to build on the capacity of religious leaders and their communities to promote peaceful intra and interfaith relationship and develop dialogue between leaders and communities. This approach will target communities most at risk of violence, fostering a culture of peace and mutual respect. Finally, the action will support mediation efforts in the Northeast, in order to explore and propose options for a political resolution of the crises.</narrative>
  </description>
